The reference is the size the queue had before this fork's floor:
RetroArch's own 9 px floor over the scaled size. On a 640x480 guest the
scaled size is 4 px, so a first cut that used the unfloored size as the
reference put the stack 3 px from the bottom (2026-09-26); the second cut
guarded that and moved nothing. Two RARCH_LOG lines say what was chosen
and what the placement became, so a frame is checked against numbers.

